# Backend Architecture (Node + TypeScript)

- Use layered module structure inside `src/modules/<domain>`:
  - `controller` for HTTP layer only
  - `service` for business logic
  - `repository` for data access
  - `validation` for request payload schemas
- Keep API composition in `src/routes/index.ts` and module route files.
- Keep app bootstrap concerns in `src/app.ts`, startup in `src/server.ts`.
- Put cross-cutting middleware only in `src/middleware`.
- Put shared helpers/errors in `src/utils`.

# Boundaries

- Controllers should not directly access repositories.
- Services should not depend on Express request/response objects.
- Validation must happen before service logic for create/update endpoints.
